there would be 73 extra
deaths per 100,000 people

00:44:26.010 --> 00:44:28.077
by 2100.

00:44:28.077 --> 00:44:30.630
So, and of course in the
middle we'll walk through that.

00:44:30.630 --> 00:44:32.170
Exclusively in poor countries

00:44:33.484 --> 00:44:36.570
and that's more than all of the death

00:44:36.570 --> 00:44:38.643
from infectious diseases today.

00:44:39.566 --> 00:44:43.260
So it's like, you know, take
all of HIV, tuberculosis,

00:44:43.260 --> 00:44:45.510
et cetera, that's going
to be more than that.

