of redistribution and so
that could also be one

01:26:05.010 --> 01:26:06.990
of the recipients of the funds

01:26:06.990 --> 01:26:08.523
that Esther was talking about.

01:26:09.511 --> 01:26:13.170
The second answer I think is
really the due flow strategy

01:26:13.170 --> 01:26:16.350
of trying to bypass existing mechanism

01:26:16.350 --> 01:26:18.603
and create new ad hoc ones.

01:26:19.678 --> 01:26:22.770
So if you add up a layer of tax
on the corporate minimum tax

01:26:22.770 --> 01:26:25.530
that is currently being
negotiated, basically no one feels

01:26:25.530 --> 01:26:27.630
that they're losing from it except

01:26:27.630 --> 01:26:30.810
a few company shareholders.

01:26:30.810 --> 01:26:34.860
But, so basically you're kind of taming

01:26:34.860 --> 01:26:37.380
down the potential losers
from such measures,

01:26:37.380 --> 01:26:39.270
but you're still generating new funds

01:26:39.270 --> 01:26:42.630
and you can use them in different
either ad hoc mechanisms

01:26:42.630 --> 01:26:45.270
in the UN, the World Bank or whatever.

01:26:45.270 --> 01:26:47.790
But that's how I think
we can progressively move

01:26:47.790 --> 01:26:49.200
beyond this national

01:26:49.200 --> 01:26:51.933
versus international
social state discussion.

01:26:53.640 --> 01:26:56.850
- Yeah, maybe kind of
without doing justice for,

01:26:56.850 --> 01:26:59.460
to all comments, so on this,

01:26:59.460 --> 01:27:01.740
I think your question cost
us very much this question,

01:27:01.740 --> 01:27:05.154
which is, the thing is
China and India became rich.

01:27:05.154 --> 01:27:08.370
A lot of people became rich.
It's not just the people below.

01:27:08.370 --> 01:27:11.340
So when we would do this
calculation is really literally

01:27:11.340 --> 01:27:14.370
what these people would consume,
but what happened in China

01:27:14.370 --> 01:27:16.140
and India, they had a lot of very, very,

01:27:16.140 --> 01:27:17.520
very rich people also.

01:27:17.520 --> 01:27:20.010
And in fact some of the
highest polluter are in China,

01:27:20.010 --> 01:27:21.690
India in term of conservation

01:27:21.690 --> 01:27:23.809
where they have their billionaire

01:27:23.809 --> 01:27:28.320
and they live in 50 floors houses

01:27:28.320 --> 01:27:31.272
and they have cars and so on and so forth.

01:27:31.272 --> 01:27:32.105
So, so that's kind of,

01:27:32.105 --> 01:27:34.010
I think the distinction between the two.

01:27:35.400 --> 01:27:37.800
So you were wondering whether
there is any precedent

01:27:37.800 --> 01:27:38.970
for international revolution?

01:27:38.970 --> 01:27:40.530
There is, we have the UN,

01:27:40.530 --> 01:27:42.603
we have the IMF, we have the World Bank.

01:27:44.133 --> 01:27:45.690
There is actually the
Bretton Wood Institution

01:27:45.690 --> 01:27:49.860
are a mechanism for global redistribution.

01:27:49.860 --> 01:27:53.850
Not very big, but nonetheless existing.

01:27:53.850 --> 01:27:55.350
That's why I was saying it's not uncommon.

01:27:55.350 --> 01:27:57.570
It's already in the system.

01:27:57.570 --> 01:28:00.951
There is pipes for
sending money for France

01:28:00.951 --> 01:28:03.840
to the World Bank and
that then that money goes

01:28:03.840 --> 01:28:05.790
to poor countries in the form of idea.

01:28:05.790 --> 01:28:08.900
So the principles are not unheard of

01:28:08.900 --> 01:28:12.000
or maybe the the magnitudes
are are different

01:28:12.000 --> 01:28:14.250
as you pointed out, you asked you,

01:28:14.250 --> 01:28:18.386
you were asking if anybody has proven

01:28:18.386 --> 01:28:21.181
that any country went out of
a poverty, poverty with ODA.

01:28:21.181 --> 01:28:23.220
First of all, I don't
think one can easily prove

01:28:23.220 --> 01:28:24.330
that one way or the other,

01:28:24.330 --> 01:28:26.880
'cause it's not that we
have a good counterfactual.

01:28:27.750 --> 01:28:32.130
Second of all, ODA is way
too small to take anybody,

01:28:32.130 --> 01:28:33.570
any country out of poverty.

01:28:33.570 --> 01:28:37.890
So even this idea would
be from richer countries,

01:28:37.890 --> 01:28:39.720
we tend to think we are so important.

01:28:39.720 --> 01:28:41.550
But in term of the budget

01:28:41.550 --> 01:28:44.760
that goes toward poor people in the world,

01:28:44.760 --> 01:28:45.780
there's this minuscule.

01:28:45.780 --> 01:28:47.640
So it's not going to
take them out of poverty

01:28:47.640 --> 01:28:48.930
if countries go out poverty,

01:28:48.930 --> 01:28:53.010
it's because of what they do and if they,

01:28:53.010 --> 01:28:58.010
or if something, if they
manage to fight the problems

01:28:58.650 --> 01:29:01.200
that people face in poor countries.

01:29:01.200 --> 01:29:02.033
So,

01:29:05.040 --> 01:29:05.940
so I kind of think

01:29:05.940 --> 01:29:09.450
that's sort of a non-question
in this particular issue.

01:29:09.450 --> 01:29:13.050
And then going back, I think it's useful

01:29:13.050 --> 01:29:16.353
to represent this idea, this money,

01:29:16.353 --> 01:29:18.060
this 500 billion.

01:29:18.060 --> 01:29:20.130
It's, I don't think it's one thing

01:29:20.130 --> 01:29:22.800
that I'm pretty convinced there
shouldn't be a counterpart

01:29:22.800 --> 01:29:25.470
that, oh, we give you this
money now you have to grow.

01:29:25.470 --> 01:29:28.140
It's not something that we
would do out of the goodness

01:29:28.140 --> 01:29:29.340
of our heart.

01:29:29.340 --> 01:29:31.890
It's something that we owe,

01:29:31.890 --> 01:29:33.900
whatever we can calculate how much we owe.

01:29:33.900 --> 01:29:37.620
We can argue on the, we
can bargain on the on,

01:29:37.620 --> 01:29:39.667
on the details, but it's not about,

01:29:39.667 --> 01:29:41.070
"Oh, I'm going to help you,

01:29:41.070 --> 01:29:43.670
but then you have to show
me you're a good student."

01:29:44.700 --> 01:29:49.170
We owe that not so much to the
countries, but to the people.

01:29:49.170 --> 01:29:51.060
And so the key difficulty

01:29:51.060 --> 01:29:52.560
is to make sure it reaches the people,

01:29:52.560 --> 01:29:54.510
whether or not the country
will grow as a result.

01:29:54.510 --> 01:29:56.250
Frankly, I think it's besides the point

01:29:56.250 --> 01:29:57.700
for this particular proposal.

01:29:58.980 --> 01:30:01.380
- Wonderful. I think we'll stop there

01:30:01.380 --> 01:30:03.030
and carry the conversation into lunch,

01:30:03.030 --> 01:30:06.030
but a warm reception for our panelists.

01:30:06.030 --> 01:30:07.459
Thank you very much.

01:30:07.459 --> 01:30:10.459
(audience clapping)

01:30:17.853 --> 01:30:20.436
(gentle music)

